      "writtenOn": "2023-06-07T17:42:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IS_ENABLED is preferred in general because it checks that the defined constant is both defined and enabled.  This is also why we shy away from things in KCONFIGS like:\nCONFIG_MKBP_USE_GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH\u003dn\n\nAnd instead prefer them to be commented out:\n\u0027# CONFIG_MKBP_USE_GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH\u003dn\u0027\n\nOur tooling still picks up that it\u0027s disabled, and errant #IF\u0027s won\u0027t fail on a definition of a \"don\u0027t use\" variable.",
      "parentUuid": "aa408e0a_4e3038b3",
      "revId": "d23fc71f300c3781b2c5ad2dd6a6436ea05fdd2f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
